      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(9\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(10\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(11\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "e",
    "value": "11"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10a-2009-p1.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\(\\dfrac{128}{12} = 10\\dfrac{2}{3},\\) ten cans hold only \\(120\\) ounces, which is not enough.\n\nTherefore \\(11\\) cans are needed.\n\nThus, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Divide \\(128\\) by \\(12\\)",
        "A partly filled last can still counts as a whole can"
      ],
